    {
      "id": "junit-basic-code",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Reject a blank journal title",
        "description": [
          "Place this learning test under src/test/java in a project with spring-boot-starter-test.",
          "A title is valid when it is not null and contains a non-whitespace character."
        ],
        "code": "import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertFalse;\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertTrue;\n\nclass TitleRules {\n    static boolean valid(String title) {\n        return title != null && !title.isBlank();\n    }\n}\n\nclass TitleRulesTest {\n    @Test\n    void acceptsVisibleText() {\n        assertTrue(TitleRules.valid(\"Morning\"));\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    void rejectsBlankTitle() {\n        assertFalse(TitleRules.valid(\"   \"));\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    void rejectsMissingTitle() {\n        assertFalse(TitleRules.valid(null));\n    }\n}",
        "language": "java",
        "explanation": [
          "The tests call TitleRules directly. No Spring application starts.",
          "Each test checks one input case.",
          "assertTrue checks the accepted title. assertFalse checks blank and missing titles.",
          "The test runner reports passing or failing tests. This code does not print application output."
        ]
      }
    },
